    "title": "Enrollment Analysis: Alaska Native students comprised 0.5% of Flagler County's only school district student body in 2023-24 school year",
    "text": "Manny Diaz,Jr., Commissioner of education at Florida Department of Education | https://www.fldoe.org/about-us/commissioner.stml\nManny Diaz,Jr., Commissioner of education at Florida Department of Education | https://www.fldoe.org/about-us/commissioner.stml\nFlorida Department of Education.\nData showed that Flagler County welcomed a total of 13,503 students at the time. Among them, Alaska Native students comprised 0.5% of the student body to be the least represented ethnicity in the county. The most represented ethnicity was white, accounting for 57.9% of the students (7,819), followed by Hispanic students who made up 18.6% of the student population (2,516).\nGov. DeSantis has approved an education budget of over $28 billion for the 2024-25 school year. The new budget includes more than $1 billion earmarked exclusively for teacher salaries to better address the teacher shortage the state faces.\nAccording to the National Education Association (NEA), Florida ranks 50th in the U.S. in terms of teacher salaries, only ahead of West Virginia.\nDistrict | No. of Alaska Native Students | Total District Enrollment | % of Total Enrollment |\n---|---|---|---|\nFlagler County School District | 64 | 13,503 | 0.5% |",
